{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/home/tests/home.test.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T05:29:39.746836Z","id":"3a33be85e361bbc0a225e0be4832dde804c24f15953808dae42dec7cffecf50a","body":{"detail":"Seen across repeated runs of web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts \"its tests in the inspect view\" (about one run in three, with the page's own entries consistent: one #group entry on the stack, no pending back). Only the test \"a tap opens the folder over a dimmed grid; its name renames; back closes it\" relies on back, as the first history use of the run, and passes steadily. The page's back handling is a single window popstate listener (home.js folderNav).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":862},"end":{"line":931},"content_hash":"07552df6cfec7cbb94a2fc6a99edb0f7e3ad7624ea305785c410c531bc8596b7"},"summary":"These folder tests close by the scrim, not history.back(): in the inspect harness's frame a script's history.back() after a script-made #group entry sometimes produced no popstate within 3 s","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
